The short-time formula [eq:l9-short-update] kept only first order in $\epsilon$. The full expansion is $e^{-i\epsilon H}
=1-i\epsilon H-\frac{\epsilon^2}{2}H^2
+\frac{i\epsilon^3}{3!}H^3+\cdots.$ At second order the Hamiltonian acts twice. This is the algebraic origin of the first compound process pictures.

